# Project Report: AI-Accelerated Phase Diagram Prediction

## 1. Executive Summary

This project establishes an integrated, AI-driven materials informatics pipeline specifically designed for the **Aluminum-Zinc (Al-Zn) binary alloy system**. Traditional thermodynamic calculations for phase diagrams (such as CALPHAD) are highly accurate but computationally expensive. This project addresses this bottleneck by generating a high-fidelity dataset using PyCALPHAD, training rapid Machine Learning (ML) surrogates to instantly predict phase stability and Gibbs free energy, and wrapping the entire system in a Streamlit web application. Furthermore, a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) engine powered by a Large Language Model (LLM) is integrated to provide scientifically rigorous thermodynamic interpretations on demand.

